  "why": "Claude Code and Pi queues live in the host's queue store (~/.dispatch/state/queue): chat.open of such a conversation reads its stored queue (storage, the store directory, the helper's own process identity, a directory watch, a private read), queue.* read and write the file, and the Mac hands queued messages to the host with queue.add. Every recording that opens a Claude Code or Pi chat asks the helper something it did not before. Found by replaying the corpus on the new helper (59 captures in these tests; nothing else changed).",
